# Fish — agent pitfalls & living lessons

Agents often write **Bash-shaped Fish**. Fish is not POSIX: different parsing, variables, and builtins. This rule applies when editing any `**/*.fish` file in this repo.

**Related (do not duplicate here):**

- [tide-report.mdc](tide-report.mdc) — project conventions, `set_color`, Fisher events, prompt rules
- [fish-scripts-lint.mdc](fish-scripts-lint.mdc) — run `fish -n` before done
- [fish-functions-no-top-level-execution.mdc](fish-functions-no-top-level-execution.mdc) — `functions/*.fish` must be definitions only

**Official references:** [Fish tutorial](https://fishshell.com/docs/current/tutorial.html), [Fish language](https://fishshell.com/docs/current/language.html).

---

## Rule to make rules (required)

When you **fix or discover** a recurring Fish mistake while working on `.fish` files in this project:

1. Add a short entry under **General (Fish ≠ Bash)** or **TideReport & tests**, with symptom, cause, bad vs good.
2. Keep entries actionable — one paragraph + minimal code.
3. Do this in the **same change** that fixes the bug or test, before marking the task done.
4. Do not duplicate entries or [tide-report.mdc](tide-report.mdc) bullets; merge if the lesson already exists.

