## TideReport & tests (project)

### Branch-scoped cache paths must match real `git` state

**Symptom:** “Warm second render” tests fail; background CI fetch; wrong `...-main-ci.json` vs `...-master-ci.json`.

**Good:** After `git init` in fixtures, seed CI cache using `git branch --show-current` (see `test/integration/github_command_counts.fish`).

### Session globals leak across Fishtape tests

**Symptom:** Test passes alone, fails in full suite.

**Cause:** Globals like `__tide_report_github_context_repo_root`, `$__tide_report_github_auth_ok` persist in one Fish process.

**Good:** `__tide_report_test_reset_github_context` before GitHub perf tests; `set -e __tide_report_github_auth_ok` after auth tests.

### Fishtape tests and subprocess noise

**Symptom:** Help text merged into `test` expression.

**Good:** `tide-report nosuch >/dev/null 2>/dev/null`; assert `$status`, not uncontrolled stdout.

**Also:** `@test` blocks must end with **only** `echo $status` on stdout—no debug `echo` lines—or Fishtape mis-parses the assertion.

### `printf` with an empty list still yields one command-substitution line

**Symptom:** `_tide_report_enabled_items` looks non-empty when no items are enabled; `count (func)` is 1.

**Cause:** `printf "%s\n" $empty_list` with no elements still produces a blank line in `( … )`.

**Good:** `test (count $enabled) -gt 0; and printf "%s\n" $enabled`

### Test setup `-g` defaults vs `set -U` in Fishtape

**Symptom:** Doctor/health tests pass in a manual shell but fail under Fishtape; provider checks see `openmeteo` instead of `typo`.

**Cause:** `test/helpers/setup.fish` applies defaults with `set -g`; a later `set -U` in the same process may not override what the check reads in a Fishtape subprocess.

**Good:** In tests, `set -e -g/-U tide_report_*` then `set -g tide_report_*` to the value under test (see `test/unit/core/health_checks.fish`).

### Fake `gh` sleep must not run on `auth status`

**Symptom:** `prompt github returns before slow fetch completes` fails on `elapsed -le 1` while weather/tide pass.

**Cause:** Missing-cache path calls `__tide_report_github_unavailable_display` → `__tide_report_github_auth_ok` → `gh auth status`. If [`test/helpers/fake_bin/gh`](../test/helpers/fake_bin/gh) sleeps before parsing argv, the prompt blocks for `TIDE_REPORT_TEST_GH_SLEEP_SECONDS`.

**Good:** Handle `auth status` first (no sleep); apply `TIDE_REPORT_TEST_GH_SLEEP_SECONDS` only for fetch-shaped `gh` invocations (`repo view`, `run list`, etc.).

### Background work vs “no I/O on second call”

**Symptom:** `jq`/`git` in log after clearing between two synchronous calls.

**Cause:** Background fetch from wrong/missing cache path or held lock under `~/.cache/tide-report/locks/`.

**Good:** Fix branch/path/policy first; do not assume only foreground code runs.

### `function &` does not background network fetches (Fish 4.x)

**Symptom:** Prompt hangs for several seconds on missing/stale cache when fake `curl`/`gh` sleeps; `_tide_item_*` takes as long as the fetch.

**Cause:** Fish documents that **functions cannot be started in the background**; `my_function &` and `begin; …; end &` run synchronously. `disown` may report “no suitable jobs”.

**Bad:**

```fish
__tide_report_fetch_github "$slug" "$cache" $timeout "$lock" &
disown 2>/dev/null
```

**Good:** Use spawn helpers or an external fish subprocess:

```fish
__tide_report_spawn_github_fetch "$slug" "$cache" $timeout "$lock"
# or: command fish $spawn_script >/dev/null 2>&1 &
```

**Exception:** `__tide_report_provider_moon_local` (offline, no network) may run inline on the prompt path.

**Reference:** [Fish job control](https://fishshell.com/docs/current/language.html#job-control); [`functions/_tide_report_spawn_helpers.fish`](functions/_tide_report_spawn_helpers.fish).

### `string match -r` on a pipe emits regex capture groups as extra lines

**Symptom:** After `fisher remove`, `tide` is “Unknown command”; prompt errors for erased `_tide_item_*` until a new session.

**Cause:** `functions --all | string match -r '…(github|weather|moon|tide)'` prints each **capture group** as a separate stdout line (`tide`, `github`, …). Those spurious names get passed to `functions --erase`, deleting Tide’s `tide` command. `tide reload` also ran after the erase, so `$_tide_left_items` stayed stale.

**Bad:**

```fish
set -l funcs (builtin functions --all | string match --entire -r '^(_*tide_report|_tide_item_(github|weather|moon|tide))')
builtin functions --erase $funcs
type -q tide && tide reload
```

**Good:** Iterate function names; reload Tide **before** erasing plugin functions:

```fish
for f in (builtin functions --all)
    string match -q --entire -r '^(_*tide_report|_tide_item_(github|weather|moon|tide))' -- $f
    and set -a funcs $f
end
type -q tide; and tide reload 2>/dev/null
builtin functions --erase $funcs
```

